Hardware: a standard laptop, free-tier cloud GPU for training, and a smartphone for testing. No special sensors required.

13. Evaluation Plan

Metrics

Classification: accuracy, precision, recall, macro-F1, confusion matrix, and calibration of confidence scores.

Decision quality: pathway accuracy and agreement with expert labels (Cohen's kappa); safety-critical recall (percentage of hazardous cases correctly routed to safe handling, target close to 100%).

User outcome: time to reach a suitable option, task success rate, and System Usability Scale (SUS) score.

Impact: estimated kg diverted and CO2e avoided per recommended action (reported as estimates).

Baselines for comparison

1.Image-only baseline: the same classifier with a fixed category-to-pathway mapping (no condition inputs).

2.Manual search baseline: users find an option using a web search and public directories.

3.General-purpose chatbot baseline: a generic LLM given the same photo and description, scored against the same expert labels.

Testing the hypothesis

Build a held-out set of at least 100 expert-labelled scenarios. Compare pathway accuracy of ReLoop AI against baselines 1 and 3 (paired comparison, McNemar's test or bootstrap confidence intervals).

Run a within-subject user study with at least 15 participants, each completing matched tasks with ReLoop AI and with manual search (order counterbalanced). Compare median task time (Wilcoxon signed-rank test) and success rate.

The hypothesis is supported if ReLoop AI meets the targeted improvements with statistical evidence. If not, we will report the results and analyse error cases.

