16. Potential Challenges and Limitations

Challenge


	Mitigation



Limited labelled e-waste images and class imbalance


	Combine public data with our own photos; augmentation; class weighting; limit to 8 categories



Visually similar items (e.g. chargers vs adapters) and poor photos


	Confidence threshold; request extra photo or manual selection



Repair feasibility varies by model and cannot be fully inferred from a photo


	Use category-level heuristics plus user inputs; label output as an estimate, not a guarantee



Safety risk from wrong advice on damaged batteries


	Hard safety overrides; conservative defaults; clear warnings



Partner data goes stale or is unverified


	Manual verification, timestamps, user feedback to flag errors; limit to a pilot city



Small user study limits statistical power


	Report confidence intervals; treat results as pilot evidence



Environmental impact estimates are approximate


	Use published averages; show ranges; avoid overclaiming



Privacy of photos and location


	Minimal data, no retention by default, informed consent



Compute limits


	Lightweight models and free-tier GPUs



Scope limits: the prototype covers selected categories and one city, does not offer data-wiping or logistics, and is a decision-support tool, not an official programme of any manufacturer or regulator.

